ategorical variables**, we check the unique values, and top categories and their frequency","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"cat_cols = train_df.select_dtypes(include=['object']).columns\n\ncat_desc = pd.DataFrame({'unique_values': train_df[cat_cols].nunique(),\n                            'top_category': train_df[cat_cols].mode().iloc[0],\n                            'top_freq_pct': [train_df[col].value_counts(normalize=True, dropna=False).iloc[0] * 100 for col in cat_cols]\n                        }).sort_values('unique_values', ascending=False)\n\ncat_desc","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:49.249227Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:49.249506Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:49.853234Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:49.249481Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:49.852654Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Summary Analysis\n\nThe dataset contains a diverse set of categorical variables describing machine specifications, operational characteristics, inventory classifications, geographical information, vendor information, and transaction metadata.\n\n#### High Cardinality Features\n\nSeveral variables contain a large number of unique values:\n\n* `TransactionDate` contains **3,676 unique dates**, indicating that transactions were recorded over a long time horizon and warrant dedicated temporal analysis.\n* `Spec_FullDescriptor` (**3,505 unique values**) and `Spec_BaseClass` (**1,249 unique values**) exhibit extremely high cardinality, reflecting substantial variation in machine models and configurations.\n* `Spec_SubClass` (**147 unique values**) and `Spec_VariantModifier` (**132 unique values**) provide additional granularity within equipment specifications.\n\nThese variables capture detailed equipment information but may require special handling due to their large number of unique categories.\n\n#### Moderate Cardinality Features\n\nVariables such as:\n\n* `FunctionalClassification` (**65 categories**)\n* `RegionCode` (**53 categories**)\n* `VendorPartnerID` (**31 categories**)\n\nprovide meaningful segmentation across machine types, geographic regions, and vendor sources.\n\nSeveral machine specification variables, including `operational_arm_reach`, `ground_contact_width`, and `wheel_tire_dimensions`, also exhibit moderate category diversity, reflecting differences in equipment design and operational characteristics.\n\n#### Low Cardinality Features\n\nMany operational and mechanical attributes contain relatively few categories:\n\n* `CabinType` (3)\n* `UtilizationTier` (3)\n* `DrivetrainType` (8)\n* `InventoryGroupCategory` (6)\n* `InventoryGroupDescription` (6)\n\n#### Category Dominance and Imbalance\n\nSeveral specification-related variables are heavily dominated by a single category, often `\"None or Unspecified\"`.\n\nExamples include:\n\n* `fluid_flow_rate` (**99.95%**)\n* `traction_system` (**99.95%**)\n* `extension_arm_layout` (**92.52%**)\n* `engine_aspiration_system` (**92.52%**)\n* `work_tool_design` (**89.21%**)\n\nThe strong concentration within these variables suggests limited variability and potentially low informational value.\n\nAdditionally, `VendorPartnerID` is notably imbalanced, with a single vendor accounting for approximately **48.9%** of all observations.\n\n#### Missing Values\n\nMissing values are concentrated primarily within machine specification attributes.\n\nVariables such as `fluid_flow_rate`, `traction_system`, `extension_arm_layout`, and `engine_aspiration_system` exhibit substantial missingness, while core business and classification variables including `RegionCode`, `FunctionalClassification`, `InventoryGroupCategory`, `InventoryGroupDescription`, and `CabinType` contain little to no missing data.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"##  Identify & Remove Duplicates\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"print(\"Duplicate rows