nsactionDate\"].dt.quarter\n\ntrain_df['AssetAge'] = train_df['TransactionYear'] - train_df['ManufactureYear']\ntrain_df[\"Intensity\"] = train_df[\"OperationalHoursMeter\"]/train_df['AssetAge']\n\n\ntest_df['TransactionDate'] = pd.to_datetime(test_df['TransactionDate'])\ntest_df['TransactionYear'] = test_df['TransactionDate'].dt.year\ntest_df['TransactionMonth'] = test_df['TransactionDate'].dt.month\ntest_df[\"TransactionQuarter\"] = test_df[\"TransactionDate\"].dt.quarter\n\ntest_df['AssetAge'] = test_df['TransactionYear'] - test_df['ManufactureYear']\ntest_df[\"Intensity\"] = test_df[\"OperationalHoursMeter\"]/test_df['AssetAge']","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.141841Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.142178Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.274176Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.142148Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.273441Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"code","source":"ftr_desc = train_df.describe().T\nftr_desc","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.275012Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.275329Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.347906Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.275308Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.347229Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Since `Intensity` goes up till inf, we will simply replace it 0. This is because, intnsity can be infinity only when there is a division by 0, meaning asset age is 0. This means that the asset is new and has not been used at all, thus Intensity = 0","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"train_df['Intensity'] = train_df['Intensity'].replace(np.inf, 0)\ntest_df['Intensity'] = test_df['Intensity'].replace(np.inf, 0)","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.348746Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.348945Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.355611Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.348926Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.354817Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Visualization","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"Visualizing some important relations that might point to some signal","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Visualization 1: Transaction Data analysis","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"fig, ax = plt.subplots(1, 3, figsize=(12, 4))\n\ntrain_df['TransactionYear'].value_counts().sort_index().plot.bar(ax=ax[0], title='Year')\ntrain_df['TransactionMonth'].value_counts().sort_index().plot.bar(ax=ax[1], title='Month')\ntrain_df['TransactionQuarter'].value_counts().sort_index().plot.bar(ax=ax[2], title='Quarter')\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.356629Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.356845Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.920214Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.356823Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.919453Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insights**:\n- Transaction volumes increase noticeably over time, with the highest activity occurring between **2008 and 2012**, particularly in **2010**.\n- Transactions are distributed throughout the year, with **February, March, and June** recording relatively higher activity than other months. However, no seasonal pattern appears as such\n- Aligning with above findings, we can see that `First` and `Second` Quarter corresponds to maximum sales","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Visualization 2: Region Distribution","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"region_counts = (train_df['RegionCode'].value_counts().head(20).sort_values())\n\nplt.figure(figsize=(10, 8))\n\nregion_counts.plot(kind='barh')\n\nplt.title('Top 20 Regions by Transaction Count')\nplt.xlabel('Number of Transactions')\nplt.ylabel('Region')\n\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.921283Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.921888Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.128179Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:51.921865Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.127497Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insights**: Transaction activity is concentrated in a few regions, with **Florida** and **Texas** accounting for the highest number of transactions by a significant margin. While transactions are recorded across many regions, the distribution is uneven, indicating stronger market activity in certain geographic areas.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Visualization 3: Target Value Distribution","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"plt.figure(figsize=(8,4))\nsns.histplot(train_df['TargetValue'], bins=40, kde=True)\nplt.title('Distribution of Target Value')\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.129184Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.129434Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.770529Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.129407Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.769521Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"**Insights**: The target variable is positively skewed, with most equipment selling at lower price ranges and a small number of high-value machines creating a long right tail.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"## Missing Value Handling","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Dropping Strategy\n\n- We will surely drop the variables that have more than 80% missing values.\n- We will also drop identifier variables like`TransactionID` and `AssetID`\n- We will also drop `TransactionDate` since we have already extracted information in form of `TransactionYear`, `TransactionMonth` and `TransactionDate`\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# cols_to_drop = missing_pct[missing_pct >= 80].index.tolist()\ncols_to_drop=['TransactionID','AssetID','TransactionDate']\n\n\ntrain_df = train_df.drop(columns=cols_to_drop)\ntest_df = test_df.drop(columns=cols_to_drop)\n\nprint(\"Dropped\", len(cols_to_drop), \"columns\")","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.771618Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.771856Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.854941Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.771835Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.85412Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":null},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"`Important Insight`: Both versions were tried, where columns having more than 80% missing values are dropped and one where no columns were dropped. The later performed better on the leaderboard, hence keeping this version without further explanation.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"#### Imputation Strategy\n\n- We will replace the missing values with a placeholder value:\n  - For numerical cols: -1\n  - For Categorical cols: 'Unknown'\n\nThese behave like signals that our model can learn and understand from, and predict what will happen if these variables are unavailable.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"`Important Insight`: Imputation with median value for numerical variables and mode for categorical variable were explored. This version yielded worse result on leaderboard, therefore, we chose constant values.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"y = train_df['TargetValue']\n\nX_train = train_df.drop(columns=['TargetValue'])\nX_test = test_df.copy()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.8559Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-26T10:34:52.856636Z","iopub.status.idle":"20